Subject: [PATCH 26/26] =?UTF-8?q?Safarium:=20Safari-style=20Add=20Bookmark?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20panel=20(=E2=8C=98D)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

⌘D (and Bookmarks > Bookmark This Tab) now opens a native popover from
the address field, or to the right of the current tab's row in the
vertical sidebar: "Add this page to: [folder]", the title, Cancel / Add.
The folder menu lists every bookmark folder, indented, with the
bookmarks-bar folder first.

Chrome adds the bookmark before asking the window to show its bubble,
so the panel keeps it only on Add (applying the title and folder);
Cancel, Escape or a click elsewhere removes it again. For a page that is
already bookmarked the panel edits that bookmark ("This page is in:",
Remove Bookmark / Done). ⌘D while the panel is open keeps it. Chrome's
bubble remains the fallback where the panel has no anchor (page full
screen).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
